  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday) \nIssued at 1126 PM CST Wed Nov 18 2026\n\nOn Saturday, a surface low will deepen over northwest Texas and \nshift eastward during the day. Southeasterly flow will ramp up and \nfrontal boundary will slip into the area late Saturday night into \nearly Sunday. A few showers or storms may develop along this frontal \nboundary, but widespread rain is not expected at this time. \n\nBy Tuesday, a reinforcing shot of even colder air arrives, along \nwith a better chance at showers and storms. Any rain should quickly \npush south Tuesday. Wednesday and into the Thanksgiving Holiday look \nmuch cooler, with temperatures likely struggling to get out of the \n50s.",
